    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Jackson Merrill**, whose 74.44 score makes him our most compelling play. Facing Grant Holmes, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a favorable matchup against a starter with a middling 4.47 xERA, and his aggressive 13% dynamic platoon boost suggests he is perfectly positioned to anchor our offensive production. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** offers elite value at 69.15, largely driven by a significant 14% park factor boost and his switch-hitting versatility, which keeps him insulated against the matchup with Jake Bennett. We are also capitalizing on the soft landing provided by Sam Aldegheri, whose 5.75 xERA significantly elevates the floors for both **Gunnar Henderson** (67.96) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57), giving us a massive projected edge in the middle of our order.\n\nDespite the depth of our starting lineup, **Nolan Schanuel** was the most difficult exclusion, finishing just outside the cut with a 49.48 score. While **Nolan Schanuel** remains a viable asset, the optimizer prioritized the higher efficiency metrics of **Dominic Smith** (53.69) and the lineup security provided by our primary starters. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Cole Carrigg**; all are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have assumed optimal placement for these hitters, any downward shift in batting order for players like **Brayan Rocchio** or **Andy Pages** could narrow their situational upside. We remain wary of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose efficiency (52.68) is currently suppressed by a tough draw against Hunter Brown; however, his power profile keeps him in the UTIL slot over bench options like **Miguel Vargas** and **Nasim Nunez**, as we hunt for consistent R and RBI output.",
